1
00:00:02,502 --> 00:00:06,567
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:08,633
Okay, act calm, act calm.

3
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:10,908
If I don't act calm, they're gonna know
something's up when I walk in there.

4
00:00:10,908 --> 00:00:12,204
Okay, easy, control your breathing.

5
00:00:12,204 --> 00:00:14,376
Breathe normally, breathe normally.

6
00:00:14,376 --> 00:00:15,200
That'll make you calm.

7
00:00:15,604 --> 00:00:16,803
Oh, God, they can see me now.

8
00:00:16,803 --> 00:00:20,065
Okay, keep against the wall and try and
walk straight past the front desk.

9
00:00:20,065 --> 00:00:22,131
Don't make eye-contact, just walk.  WALK!

10
00:00:22,131 --> 00:00:23,252
GUARD: Hey, Mr. Freeman.
DAMMIT!

11
00:00:23,252 --> 00:00:27,019
GUARD: I had a bunch of messages for you,
but we had a system crash about 20 minutes ago

12
00:00:27,019 --> 00:00:28,560
GUARD: and I'm still trying to find my files.

13
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:29,569
I was so close!

14
00:00:29,569 --> 00:00:30,799
GUARD: Just one of those days, I guess.

15
00:00:30,799 --> 00:00:33,217
GUARD: They were having some problems
down in the Test Chamber, too,

16
00:00:33,217 --> 00:00:35,170
GUARD: but, I think that's all
straightened out.

17
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:36,804
GUARD: They told me to make sure
you headed down there

18
00:00:36,804 --> 00:00:38,396
GUARD: as soon as you got
into your hazard suit.

19
00:00:38,396 --> 00:00:39,345
Really?

20
00:00:39,345 --> 00:00:40,722
Maybe I'm not fired.

21
00:00:40,722 --> 00:00:44,651
In that case, let me show you what a
genius I am and look at your computer.

22
00:00:44,651 --> 00:00:46,909
SCIENTIST: Someone has hidden
my glasses again.

23
00:00:46,909 --> 00:00:47,868
Uh, yeah.

24
00:00:48,343 --> 00:00:50,033
Let's see.

25
00:00:50,033 --> 00:00:52,969
Wait a minute, this is a
Windows blue screen.

26
00:00:52,969 --> 00:00:55,500
And you're typing on it like you
know what you're doing.

27
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:56,609
You're not doing anything.

28
00:00:56,609 --> 00:00:57,406
SCIENTIST: Let me help you.

29
00:00:57,406 --> 00:00:58,426
Shut up!

30
00:00:58,426 --> 00:01:02,026
You're just looking busy. That's your
whole job, isn't it? Looking busy.

31
00:01:02,026 --> 00:01:03,934
Look, you have to reboot it.

32
00:01:03,934 --> 00:01:05,167
Where's the reset button?

33
00:01:05,167 --> 00:01:05,822
Is this it?

34
00:01:05,822 --> 00:01:07,812
[alarm sounds]
SCIENTIST: My God! What are you doing?

35
00:01:07,812 --> 00:01:08,829
Well, that's not it.

36
00:01:08,829 --> 00:01:11,779
GUARD: C'mon, Gordon! You tryin'
to get me into trouble?

37
00:01:11,779 --> 00:01:14,410
Okay, you can all go to hell if
you're gonna act like that.

38
00:01:14,410 --> 00:01:16,889
See if I ever do anything
nice for you again.

39
00:01:16,889 --> 00:01:18,247
Because I won't.

40
00:01:18,247 --> 00:01:19,581
SCIENTIST: As I expected.

41
00:01:19,581 --> 00:01:20,500
WHAT WAS THAT?!

42
00:01:21,016 --> 00:01:22,634
You tryin' to say somethin' about me?!

43
00:01:24,407 --> 00:01:25,601
Man, I'll kill you!

44
00:01:26,170 --> 00:01:27,033
Pricks...

45
00:01:27,601 --> 00:01:30,374
Well, they've got some lip up in
here, I'll say that much.

46
00:01:30,374 --> 00:01:32,934
Makes me wonder what else
they're saying behind my back.

47
00:01:33,977 --> 00:01:35,708
Well, it doesn't matter.

48
00:01:35,708 --> 00:01:37,482
I could take on any of them.

49
00:01:37,482 --> 00:01:38,330
SCIENTIST: Freeman.

50
00:01:38,330 --> 00:01:39,642
'sup, fool?

51
00:01:39,642 --> 00:01:42,133
Man, someday I'm gonna own this place.

52
00:01:43,223 --> 00:01:45,122
Wup, there's management.

53
00:01:45,122 --> 00:01:47,429
Let me guess what they're talking about.

54
00:01:47,429 --> 00:01:52,356
"You, sir, are mad! Dinosaurs are
reptiles! They must be cold-blooded!"

55
00:01:52,356 --> 00:01:55,138
"Now, you listen and you listen good:

56
00:01:55,138 --> 00:01:59,672
"Birds are one of the closest living
relatives to dinosaurs we have.

57
00:01:59,672 --> 00:02:02,741
"And I don't need to tell you
they're all warm-blooded."

58
00:02:02,741 --> 00:02:07,434
"Do you know how difficult it is to maintain
thermostasis for an animal so large?

59
00:02:07,434 --> 00:02:09,193
"They're cold-blooded, I tell you!"

60
00:02:09,193 --> 00:02:10,461
"Let me tell you something.

61
00:02:10,461 --> 00:02:14,354
"There's evidence to suggest
that velociraptors had feathers.

62
00:02:14,354 --> 00:02:16,927
"Feathers! Now, what does that tell you?"

63
00:02:16,927 --> 00:02:20,312
All right, this is stupid. I may
as well go to work.

64
00:02:20,312 --> 00:02:22,031
I'm glad I'm not fired.

65
00:02:22,031 --> 00:02:24,525
That means I don't have to
loot the place.

66
00:02:24,525 --> 00:02:28,497
Stealing from work is so much more stressful
than not stealing from work.

67
00:02:28,497 --> 00:02:30,067
There's just no comparison.

68
00:02:30,768 --> 00:02:31,931
Move it, blue stuff.

69
00:02:31,931 --> 00:02:33,878
GUARD: I think you got the wrong
airlock, Mr. Freeman.

70
00:02:33,878 --> 00:02:35,178
GUARD: You know I can't let you
through here.

71
00:02:35,178 --> 00:02:35,734
Uh...

72
00:02:36,595 --> 00:02:37,467
I knew that.

73
00:02:39,449 --> 00:02:41,200
This is kinda awkward...

74
00:02:41,852 --> 00:02:43,634
Did I really go the wrong way?

75
00:02:44,356 --> 00:02:47,234
Yep, there it is: Sector B.

76
00:02:47,234 --> 00:02:49,534
Man, I am tripping this morning!

77
00:02:52,136 --> 00:02:55,801
Wait a second, did I see
what I think I did?

78
00:02:57,868 --> 00:03:02,438
Yep, I sure did--Newton's
formula for gravitational force.

79
00:03:02,438 --> 00:03:05,428
Having trouble remembering
that one, guys?

80
00:03:05,428 --> 00:03:08,028
What is this? Are we back in
high school now?

81
00:03:08,028 --> 00:03:10,844
My department is working on
quantum displacement.

82
00:03:10,844 --> 00:03:12,843
Just what the hell are you guys doing?

83
00:03:12,843 --> 00:03:15,834
Jerking around in labcoats from
the looks of things.

84
00:03:16,498 --> 00:03:21,207
I just can't believe it. Those monkeys in there
are having trouble learning about gravity,

85
00:03:21,207 --> 00:03:26,827
whereas I can recite the quantum chromodynamic
gauge invariant Lagrangian in my sleep!

86
00:03:26,827 --> 00:03:28,367
There is no justice.

87
00:03:30,344 --> 00:03:31,783
[muffled music]
Am I hearing things?

88
00:03:31,783 --> 00:03:34,059
[muffled music]

89
00:03:34,059 --> 00:03:35,699
[blaring techno music]

90
00:03:35,699 --> 00:03:39,408
[blaring techno music]
TURN DOWN THE MUSIC, YOU FRIGGIN' BASSHEADS!

91
00:03:39,408 --> 00:03:44,092
[blaring techno music]
IT SOUNDS LIKE A STRIP CLUB IN HERE! GOD DAMN!

92
00:03:44,092 --> 00:03:47,979
[blaring techno music]
JUST GET SOME DANCING GIRLS IN CAGES, WHY DON'T YOU?

93
00:03:47,979 --> 00:03:49,279
[blaring techno music]
GOOD LORD!

94
00:03:49,279 --> 00:03:50,818
[blaring techno music]

95
00:03:50,818 --> 00:03:53,605
[techno music fades]
MAN! Programmers...

96
00:03:53,605 --> 00:03:55,567
Who knows what they're doing in there?

97
00:03:56,260 --> 00:03:59,373
They're going to go deaf before the
end of the year at that rate.

98
00:03:59,373 --> 00:04:02,254
Next time I have to go in there,
I'll bring some ear protection.

99
00:04:02,254 --> 00:04:03,701
SCIENTIST: Ah, it's good to see you.

100
00:04:04,111 --> 00:04:04,611
What?

101
00:04:04,967 --> 00:04:06,378
Is he talking to me?

102
00:04:06,378 --> 00:04:08,033
He's not even looking this way.

103
00:04:08,914 --> 00:04:10,801
I could've sworn I heard something...

104
00:04:11,775 --> 00:04:13,368
Ah, I'm losing my mind.

105
00:04:13,368 --> 00:04:17,133
Well, at least it sounded friendly,
unlike that prick back at the lobby.

106
00:04:18,951 --> 00:04:21,000
"This place is dead..."

107
00:04:21,851 --> 00:04:25,849
Oh! I see a bowl of
noodles with my name on it.

108
00:04:25,849 --> 00:04:26,964
Okay, I can do this.

109
00:04:26,964 --> 00:04:30,174
The guy on the left isn't looking but the
guy on the right is a rogue element.

110
00:04:30,174 --> 00:04:30,975
Uh...

111
00:04:30,975 --> 00:04:32,412
Uh-oh, he's walking towards me.

112
00:04:32,412 --> 00:04:34,200
Stay cool, stay cool.

113
00:04:35,194 --> 00:04:37,242
Oh, man, this guy's a pro.

114
00:04:37,242 --> 00:04:39,204
I can't compete with this!

115
00:04:39,204 --> 00:04:41,467
I shouldn't have hesitated; I had it!

116
00:04:42,043 --> 00:04:45,750
Oh well, I guess I'll have to grab
something else for breakfast,

117
00:04:45,750 --> 00:04:49,131
like some oxycodone!

118
00:04:49,131 --> 00:04:53,236
I think it's time to go visit my
locker, get some happy pills

119
00:04:53,236 --> 00:04:56,203
and make the politics here
just float away.

120
00:04:56,203 --> 00:04:59,707
SCIENTIST: Why do we all have to
wear these ridiculous ties?

121
00:04:59,707 --> 00:05:00,939
Oh, you wanna know why?

122
00:05:00,939 --> 00:05:01,915
I'll tell you why.

123
00:05:01,915 --> 00:05:03,240
It's symbolic.

124
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:05,767
The management wants you to know
that you're their dog,

125
00:05:05,767 --> 00:05:07,889
so you're wearing their leash.

126
00:05:07,889 --> 00:05:09,870
You don't see me wearing a tie, do you?

127
00:05:09,870 --> 00:05:10,857
You know why?

128
00:05:10,857 --> 00:05:11,767
Because I'm a rebel.

129
00:05:12,145 --> 00:05:14,405
The day they tried to enforce
the dress code on me,

130
00:05:14,405 --> 00:05:17,612
I let them know there could be an
accident around here if that happened.

131
00:05:17,612 --> 00:05:20,469
And by 'accident', I mean
'bomb the place'.

132
00:05:20,469 --> 00:05:22,322
Hey, are you even listening?

133
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:23,381
Eh, forget you.

134
00:05:23,381 --> 00:05:26,080
My voice falls on deaf ears.

135
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:28,891
I don't even know why I waste
my time on you sheep.

136
00:05:28,891 --> 00:05:31,522
I wonder if Feynman felt the same way.

137
00:05:31,522 --> 00:05:32,782
What the hell?

138
00:05:32,782 --> 00:05:34,576
Whose stuff is this?

139
00:05:34,576 --> 00:05:37,259
There's my name, but...

140
00:05:37,259 --> 00:05:42,825
But, here's a bowling certificate,
baby pictures, blue poncho...?

141
00:05:42,825 --> 00:05:44,868
WHERE'S ALL MY STUFF?!

142
00:05:44,868 --> 00:05:46,695
WHERE'S MY STASH?!

143
00:05:46,695 --> 00:05:49,234
This is freaking me out.

144
00:05:49,234 --> 00:05:52,874
It's like everything's backwards,
and I'm not even left-handed.

145
00:05:53,685 --> 00:05:58,267
Okay, I'm just gonna go to work
and hope all these problems go away.

146
00:05:58,703 --> 00:05:59,267
Yeah.

147
00:05:59,846 --> 00:06:03,200
Oh, come on!
Now somebody's taken my helmet!

148
00:06:04,323 --> 00:06:06,602
Eh, screw it, I probably won't
need it anyway.

149
00:06:06,602 --> 00:06:10,381
HEV: Welcome to the HEV Mark 4
Oh no, there's that voice.

150
00:06:10,381 --> 00:06:12,448
HEV: Protective System.

151
00:06:12,448 --> 00:06:15,916
HEV: For use in hazardous
environment conditions.

152
00:06:15,916 --> 00:06:16,514
Shh!

153
00:06:16,514 --> 00:06:20,585
HEV: High-impact reactive armor: activated;

154
00:06:20,585 --> 00:06:24,649
HEV: Atmospheric contaminant
sensors: activated;

155
00:06:24,649 --> 00:06:25,187
Quiet!

156
00:06:25,187 --> 00:06:28,517
HEV: Vital sign monitoring: activated;

157
00:06:28,517 --> 00:06:31,398
HEV: Automatic medical systems: engaged;

158
00:06:31,398 --> 00:06:33,337
Wow, this suit does not shut up.

159
00:06:33,337 --> 00:06:36,034
HEV: Defensive weapon selection
system: activated;

160
00:06:36,034 --> 00:06:39,633
HEV: Munition level monitoring: activated;

161
00:06:39,633 --> 00:06:43,395
HEV: Communications interface: online;
Okay, this thing's ridiculous,

162
00:06:43,395 --> 00:06:44,623
HEV: Have a very sa--
where's the 'off' button?

163
00:06:44,623 --> 00:06:46,440
[beep]
There we go.

164
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:50,186
Huh, didn't it say,
"Munitions level monitoring"?

165
00:06:50,186 --> 00:06:51,475
What does that mean?

166
00:06:51,475 --> 00:06:54,322
Does the left hand turn into a chaingun?

167
00:06:54,322 --> 00:06:55,488
I wish!

168
00:06:55,488 --> 00:06:58,204
GUARD: Go right on through, sir.
Looks like you're in the barrel today.

169
00:06:58,204 --> 00:06:59,074
Oh!

170
00:06:59,074 --> 00:07:02,319
Did he just say I'm in the barrel today?

171
00:07:02,319 --> 00:07:04,634
Oooh, shit!

172
00:07:04,634 --> 00:07:08,728
Looks like I'm not the only person
here who knows some dirty jokes.

173
00:07:08,728 --> 00:07:12,709
"You're in the barrel..."
I can't believe he said that.

174
00:07:12,709 --> 00:07:18,289
I bet he says that to the other scientists
and it goes right over their head.

175
00:07:18,289 --> 00:07:21,734
He probably thinks I don't know
what it means either, but I do.

